    const exam = state.exams.find(item => item.id === target.id);
    if (!exam) return undefined;
    exam.review ||= { version: 1, receipts: [], responses: [] };
    return { read: () => exam.review!.receipts, write: receipts => { exam.review!.receipts = receipts; } };
  }
  ...tutor...
};
```

That keeps `persistReceipts` and `saveReviewCheckpoints` working for exams (checkpoints too — needed? `startUnitAudit` uses checkpoints; for exam it would write per-role checkpoint receipts as checks finish, which is good for resumability).

Hmm wait, checkpoints: `saveReviewCheckpoints(draft, store, unit.revision, ...)` writes `reviewCheckpoint(contentHash, sourceHash, ctx, role, batches)` for roles "source"|"teaching"|"visual". For exam the roles are "assessment"|"teaching" — checkpoint's `save(role: ReviewPacketRole, batches)` guard: `if (closed || (role !== "source" && role !== "teaching" && role !== "visual")) return;`. So assessment checkpoints are dropped; teaching checkpoints are saved as `reviewCheckpoint(... role="teaching" ...)`. Hmm, a teaching checkpoint has `failure.code = "cancelled"` and status "changes" — writing it as a receipt for the exam revision means `unitReviewFailures` would report... wait, checkpoints have `failure: {code: "cancelled", message: REVIEW_CHECKPOINT_MESSAGE}`. For Learn, these exist too. `pruneReviewReceipts` drops a `cancelled` checkpoint once the role+content group has a completed receipt. And `unitAudited` requires `!receipt.failure`. OK.

