However: `persistReceipts` uses `pruneReviewReceipts([...quality.read(), ...receipts], {sourceHash, model})`, and `reviewerModelName(ctx)` is the model bound at write time. OK.

Should I use checkpoints for exam? It adds resumability for long exam audits (many packets). `startUnitAudit` does it uniformly. Keep it uniform — less special-casing. Tests: the obsidian test's first check asserts `receipts.every(receipt => receipt.status === "pass")`. With checkpoint receipts... after a successful audit, checkpoints for teaching role with a completed teaching receipt → pruned. Assessment checkpoints never saved. So all remaining receipts are "pass". Good.

Wait, one more: `receipts.every(receipt => receipt.contentHash === frozenFingerprint)`. The checkpoint contentHash = unit.revision = formHash; final receipts contentHash = unit.revision. Good. But careful: `pruneReviewReceipts` with `model` — checkpoints use `reviewerModelName(ctx)` same as receipts. OK.

Now, `persistReceipts` guard: `if (activation !== session.state || !ports.isActiveAuthority(state) || state.source.fingerprint.sha256 !== sourceHash) return;` — fine.

